  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions. Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene, and Chaxamycin B, which all ultimately target CCF-STTG1. These findings indicate that Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate may serve as a substrate or a point of interaction for various compounds that modulate the activity of CCF-STTG1. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate influences CCF-STTG1 remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible regulatory pathway involving sialyltransferases and their interaction with bioactive compounds, but further experimental validation is needed to establish a definitive causal link.",
